[16/19] Interpretation lock...
1. After semantic distance from the seed is controlled, the TEST123 relationship between local probe score and terminal transport largely disappears.
2. The earlier signal was therefore substantially explained by angular proximity to the fixed semantic seed.
3. The current one-step transport score should not yet be used as a feedback-controller sensor.
4. TEST124 is a system-identification characterization assay because all 24 candidates receive terminal evaluation.
5. No exact derivative or Jacobian is measured; all local responses are finite perturbation responses.
6. No physical force, momentum, resistance, or energy quantity is claimed.
7. No manifold-recovery claim is made.
8. No behavioral efficacy claim is made.
9. No semantic-causality claim is made.
10. The TEST124 prompts are exposed after this successful run and must not be reused as future blind validation.

